  "pli-tv-bi-vb-pj7:2.1.10": "Sp 2.669: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Dhammenāti bhūtena vatthunā. Vinayenāti codetvā sāretvā. Padabhājanaṁ panassa “yena dhammena yena vinayena ukkhitto suukkhitto hotī”ti imaṁadhippāyamattaṁ dassetuṁ vuttaṁ</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Dhammena</i>: according to truth, according to the rule. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Vinayena</i>: having accused, having reminded. But the word analysis is spoken to show just this meaning: ‘<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Yena dhammena yena vinayena</i> means ejected, properly ejected.’” ",
